  "problem": "Reviewers could be asked to approve an unspecified whole dataset. Accepting one field could silently accept others. Identical evidence grouping could merge separate source identities. Stale approvals could survive revised source bytes. Pending proposals could be described as public facts. Existing identity-candidate queues could be broken.",
  "resulting_behavior": "buildClaimReviewPacket shows before/after, release/context, cited passage, parser/model versions, disagreements and affected products/examples. Packet hashes bind the precise values reviewed. Identical evidence is grouped without merging source identities. A reviewer can accept one field while leaving others unresolved. Dispositions are accept, reject, request evidence and supersede. Units, denominators, grain and identity conflicts have higher priority. Revised source bytes or changed proposals invalidate stale decisions. Queue reports age, cause, owners and accepted/rejected counts. Pending proposals are never public facts. Whole-dataset approval is forbidden. Existing identity-candidate buildReviewQueue behavior is preserved. schema-catalog.mjs remains 16653 bytes.",
